      "text": "Assessment summaries",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "heading_path": [
        "Assessment summaries"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In: Procure > Clarification and due diligence",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "Assessment summaries"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Overview",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "Assessment summaries",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The guidance documents are intended to provide technical guidance and help with interpretation and understanding of the Procurement Act 2023.",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "Assessment summaries",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The guidance documents should be read in conjunction with the Procurement Act 2023 and its associated regulations and are aimed at procurement practitioners and commercial policy leads in contracting authorities. They are intended to provide technical guidance and help with interpretation and understanding of the Procurement Act 2023.",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "Assessment summaries",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Under the Procurement Act 2023 (Act), before entering into a public contract, a contracting authority must generally publish a contract award notice (section 50(1)) on the central digital platform. The contract award notice triggers the commencement of the mandatory standstill period.",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "Assessment summaries",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In addition, where a contracting authority has carried out a competitive tendering procedure under the Act, it must, prior to publishing the contract award notice, provide an ‘assessment summary’ which provides information to enable a relevant supplier to understand why its tender was either successful or unsuccessful.",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "Assessment summaries",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "When awarding a contract following a competitive tendering procedure, a contracting authority must provide an assessment summary to each supplier that submitted an ‘assessed tender’ and publish a contract award notice.",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "Assessment summaries",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
